% The contract the charity must file its annual return starts: its first obligations.
when the contract the charity must file its annual return starts on day a day with charity a charity
    and the status of the charity is a value
    and the value is equal to active
    and a due day = day + 60
then the charity must file its annual return obliges the_charity to file the annual return by day the due day as its first obligation.

when the contract the charity must file its annual return starts on day a day with charity a charity
    and the status of the charity is a value
    and the value is different from active
then the contract is fulfilled.

% The first obligation of the charity must file its annual return: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does file the annual return on day a day
    and the charity must file its annual return obliges the party to file the annual return by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the charity must file its annual return obliges the party to file the annual return by day the due day as its first obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the charity must file its annual return obliges a party to file the annual return by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the charity must file its annual return permits the_commissioner to issue a required steps notice as its second obligation
    and it is not the case that the charity must file its annual return obliges the party to file the annual return by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The second obligation of the charity must file its annual return: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does issue a required steps notice on day a day
    and the charity must file its annual return permits the party to issue a required steps notice as its second obligation
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the charity must file its annual return permits the party to issue a required steps notice as its second obligation.

